From: Brian 'redbeard' Harrington <redbeard@dead-city.org>
Subject: [PATCH] opensbi: vendored K3 suspend-tree manifest (baseline b4152e0 + quiet-deny pin 51a9d0f9)

NOT AN APPLIED PATCH. sources.lock.json pins the opensbi component
by revision with an EMPTY patch list; this file is that component's
manifest and the evidence anchor cited by
docs/audit-2026-11-20/standards.csv. It replaces the hand-written
pseudocode patch that was not git-applicable (audit finding 1,
2026-11-20).

  component:  opensbi
  revision:   51a9d0f99d23aa00ad9d14c84874c4673d9559ac  (lock pin)
  repository: workdir/k3-maintained-efi/opensbi-controller-trace-diagnostic (local)

The component is a vendored local snapshot — no clean upstream
identity survives (the tree predates the repo-qualification
discipline), and the repository field is a local absolute path:
reproduction requires this workstation until the tree is published.

History of the pinned tree (two commits):

  b4152e07  BASELINE IMPORT — the spacemit K3 OpenSBI tree as staged
            during this project, squashed at the v21g state
            (fw_dynamic sha256 2f14c5c85bf91e1c..., the
            hardware-qualified v21g/v21h cycles). Contains, relative
            to the vendor tree:
              P0 batches  explicit suspend-type dispatch; genuine
                          type-0 WFI before any vote/mask/IMSIC/
                          cache change; backend error propagation
                          with the hart/type/error diagnostic
              v15 fix     dispatch hoist: type validation precedes
                          every hardware change (zero CSR/PMU
                          writes on rejection)
              v16 fix     ENOTSUPP-fallback translation: the
                          wrapper fails NON_RET_DEFAULT outright so
                          sbi_hsm cannot consume ENOTSUPP as a
                          generic-fallback request (the v14/v15
                          hart wedges)
              v21         K3_HSM_SUSP_CLUSTER_RET (0x11000000)
                          routed through RPMI_HSM_SRV_HART_SUSPEND
                          (k3_rpmi_hsm_route_suspend): deny
                          pre-hardware; grant = plain WFI (the v21f
                          corruption panic fixed — a grant licenses
                          no per-hart vote)

  51a9d0f9  QUIET-DENY FIX — the current pin. The rpmi-hsm deny
            print fired from the idle path at cpuidle retry
            frequency; five harts printing every denial saturated
            the 115200-baud console and took the network down (the
            first LPI-2 flash, 2026-11-20). Rate-limited to ONCE
            PER HART: the error code returned to the caller is the
            durable signal; the console line is a boot-time aid
            (the transition-path serial rule applied to the print
            that predated it). Shipped in the lpi2q image
            (pico-acpi-lpi2q-20261121): sealed opensbi partition
            sha256 a8e5b7a3b189b246..., fw_dynamic embedded in it
            sha256 32947c880b6b5a1a... (quiet-deny string verified
            present in the sealed payload by FIT walk).

The diff below is the verbatim b4152e0..51a9d0f9 delta,
git-apply-able onto the baseline import, so the pinned change is
reviewable without the local vendored tree.

Future OpenSBI changes diff against the pinned commit and ship as
numbered patches in this directory; the component revision advances
with each qualified cycle.

diff --git a/lib/utils/hsm/fdt_hsm_rpmi.c b/lib/utils/hsm/fdt_hsm_rpmi.c
index cdbdef1..7ac90bf 100644
--- a/lib/utils/hsm/fdt_hsm_rpmi.c
+++ b/lib/utils/hsm/fdt_hsm_rpmi.c
@@ -128,9 +128,27 @@ static int rpmi_hsm_suspend(u32 type, ulong resume_addr)
 	 * failed suspends were reported to the SBI caller as success.
 	 */
 	rc = __rpmi_hsm_suspend(type);
-	if (rc)
-		sbi_printf("rpmi-hsm: hart %u suspend type %#x failed: %d\n",
-			   current_hartid(), type, rc);
+	/*
+	 * TRANSITION-PATH SERIAL RULE (the LPI-2 lesson): this print
+	 * fires from the idle path — a cpuidle state backed by a
+	 * denied suspend retries at IDLE FREQUENCY. An unbounded print
+	 * here floods the console and starves the system (the first
+	 * LPI-2 flash lost the network to exactly this). Print ONCE
+	 * per hart per type: the error code returned to the caller is
+	 * the durable signal; the console line is a boot-time aid.
+	 */
+	{
+		static unsigned long reported;
+		unsigned long bit = 1UL << (current_hartid() % 64);
+
+		if (!(reported & bit)) {
+			reported |= bit;
+			sbi_printf("rpmi-hsm: hart %u suspend type %#x "
+				   "failed: %d (once; further denials are "
+				   "silent)\n",
+				   current_hartid(), type, rc);
+		}
+	}
 
 	/*
 	 * HARDWARE-VALIDATED FIX (v15 phase-A): sbi_hsm_hart_suspend()
